## Executive Summary (≤150 words)
Receivable Details: A total of EUR 4,500,000 is scheduled to be received in 90 days.
FX Risk: As a USD-reporting entity, our primary risk is depreciation of the EUR. If the Euro weakens against the Dollar during this 90-day window, the converted USD cash flow will shrink, potentially threatening project margins and budget allocations.
Business Context: This receivable represents a significant portion of quarterly revenue. Given the current volatility in Eurozone interest rate policy, the hedging decision is driven by the need for cash-flow predictability versus the desire to participate in any potential Eurozone recovery.
