### C. Sensitivity Interpretation

Our Stage 2 model demonstrates a clear "divergence of outcomes" based on a ±5% EUR movement:
EUR Depreciation (-5%): In a "bear" scenario, the Forward and Money Market hedges are the clear winners, outperforming an unhedged position by roughly $225,000. The Put Option successfully triggers its floor, protecting the firm from the worst-case scenario.
EUR Appreciation (+5%): If the EUR strengthens, the Forward hedge becomes a "regret" position, as we are locked into the lower rate. The Put Option shines here; we let the option expire worthless and sell EUR at the higher market spot rate, capturing the gain (minus the initial premium).
